{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'rg --files task/resources; cat results/ideas/03_endpoint_contrast_sure_for_exposure_regression/idea_bundle.json; cat results/ideas/03_endpoint_contrast_sure_for_exposure_regression/program_1/rubric_status.json; ls -l results/ideas/02_nonbacktracking_two_hop_regression_with_invariant_gcv/program_1/; cat results/ideas/02_nonbacktracking_two_hop_regression_with_invariant_gcv/program_1/harness_evaluate_stderr.log'","aggregated_output":"task/resources/search/manifest.json\ntask/resources/search/benchmark.npz\ntask/resources/final/benchmark.npz\ntask/resources/final/Stanford3.zip\ntask/resources/final/manifest.json\n{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Selecting regularization for the all-treated minus all-control contrast, rather than observed-outcome prediction error, can improve regression GATE estimation when noisy, weakly supported exposure directions dominate endpoint error. A small quadratic exposure reference permits an observed-data contrast-risk estimate under an explicitly assumed correctly specified linear reference with independent homoskedastic Gaussian noise. This is a testable shrinkage heuristic, not a claim of identification under arbitrary interference or an unbiased post-selection risk guarantee.\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"cycle03_endpoint_contrast_sure\",\n  \"implementation_plan\": [\n    \"Start from the validated incumbent and preserve ingestion, reset, fit/predict dispatch, response keys and resource limits; do not infer a defect from cycle 2's unavailable failure cause.\",\n    \"Keep the incumbent feature/fit path as fallback. Add a fixed reference with intercept, supplied covariates, own treatment z, one-hop treated-neighbor fraction e, z*e, e*(1-e), and z*e*(1-e); isolates retain e=0.\",\n    \"Build observed and both endpoint reference designs from the same graph routine. Center and scale non-intercept columns using observed-design statistics, and compute the mean endpoint feature contrast in those coordinates.\",\n    \"Take a thin SVD of the standardized observed design. Check that the endpoint contrast lies in its retained row space and that positive residual degrees of freedom remain; otherwise return the unchanged incumbent model.\",\n    \"Form the reference contrast weights and residual noise estimate. Evaluate only the fixed five-penalty ridge grid with the contrast-risk criterion in the rubrics, retain signed risk estimates, and select the first finite minimum deterministically.\",\n    \"Store the selected ridge coefficients and observed-data preprocessing; predict all three assignments with that same model. Bypass fitting for exactly constant outcomes and return three identical constant rows.\",\n    \"In the authorized execution stage, compare the incumbent, the same reference with observed-outcome GCV, and endpoint-risk tuning under matched seeds; report bias, RMSE, Monte Carlo uncertainty, fallback frequency and negative results without extra RPC response fields.\",\n    \"For the broader research deliverable, prespecify sparse/dense SBM and degree-heterogeneous graphs, optional permitted public graphs, polynomial versus threshold/two-hop interference, and independent versus graph-correlated noise; treat unrun studies and the paper/PDF as outstanding.\"\n  ],\n  \"notes_for_agent\": \"This is a new estimator hypothesis, not a repair diagnosis. Cycle 1 preserved incumbent predictions and tied its score; cycle 2 has no established acceptance or scientific comparison because its run exited with cause unavailable. Do not turn either fact into evidence against two-hop regression or a claimed protocol bug. The documented candidate interface supplies only graph edges, covariates, observed assignment/outcomes and a seed; candidate controls are model fitting and the three prediction rows. There are no assignment-design probabilities, endpoint truths, case labels, training trajectories, internal telemetry or artifact-exchange controls. Use only these observations, no external reads inside the candidate and no added response fields. Preserve the incumbent _features path and implement _fit_incumbent so every ineligible reference branch remains a real usable model. The reference has centered outcome y-y.mean(), observed-only column means/scales, a thin SVD and an unpenalized intercept. Reference weights are the minimum-norm linear unbiased weights only when the checked contrast is estimable under the stated reference; a pseudoinverse alone does not identify it. Estimate residual noise using projection onto retained left singular vectors, and reject nonpositive residual degrees of freedom or nonfinite scores. Set nonfinite candidate risks to infinity and fall back if all are nonfinite. The selected ridge coefficients must use exactly the retained SVD and penalty used in the contrast weights, with no endpoint-specific refitting or post-hoc contrast editing. For each fixed penalty, the risk formula is justified under a correct linear mean and iid Gaussian errors with the residual variance estimate independent of the fitted projection; selection among estimated risks is itself noisy and does not inherit unbiased risk reporting. Threshold spillovers, omitted two-hop effects, graph-correlated errors and exposure concentration can invalidate that rationale, and estimability is not endpoint support. Evaluate those as failures, not as exceptions to hide. Compare endpoint-risk tuning against GCV on the SAME reference basis to isolate tuning from representation changes. No numeric score threshold beyond the harness gate is authored. Source snippets must occur in called program_1/src code. This idea stage performs no candidate/evaluator execution or numerical probes and asserts no new measured improvement. Maintain the full research deliverable requirements separately; a successful RPC candidate is not the completed paper. Do not search for, infer or access the prohibited paper or derivative pages. Canonical idea memory is ../../ideas/03_endpoint_contrast_sure_for_exposure_regression/memory.md.\",\n  \"target_rubrics\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"combined_score > 0.9909514004064053\",\n      \"id\": \"incumbent_score_improvement\",\n      \"metric\": \"combined_score\",\n      \"operator\": \">\",\n      \"threshold\": 0.9909514004064053,\n      \"type\": \"metric\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Actually fit a fixed low-dimensional reference containing supplied covariates, treatment, one-hop exposure, their product and endpoint-zero curvature terms. Use graph-consistent endpoint designs, including zero exposure at isolates, and observed-only feature scaling for the endpoint contrast.\",\n      \"id\": \"endpoint_anchored_reference_features\",\n      \"type\": \"implementation\",\n      \"verification\": {\n        \"patterns\": [\n          \"curvature = exposure * (1.0 - exposure)\",\n          \"return np.column_stack((np.ones(_state['n']), _state['x'], assignment, exposure, assignment * exposure, curvature, assignment * curvature))\",\n          \"endpoint_contrast = (treated_design[:, 1:].mean(axis=0) - control_design[:, 1:].mean(axis=0)) / feature_scale\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"source_contains\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Check endpoint-contrast estimability in the retained SVD row space before treating the reference as unbiased. Require positive residual degrees of freedom and finite numerical quantities; otherwise use the incumbent fit. Compute reference weights and the residual noise estimate only on the eligible branch.\",\n      \"id\": \"estimable_reference_and_noise_guard\",\n      \"type\": \"implementation\",\n      \"verification\": {\n        \"patterns\": [\n          \"retained = singular_values > max(standardized_design.shape) * np.finfo(np.float64).eps * singular_values[0]\",\n          \"contrast_coordinates = right_vectors[retained] @ endpoint_contrast\",\n          \"estimability_error = np.linalg.norm(endpoint_contrast - right_vectors[retained].T @ contrast_coordinates)\",\n          \"if estimability_error > 1e-8 * max(1.0, np.linalg.norm(endpoint_contrast)):\",\n          \"reference_weights = left_vectors[:, retained] @ (contrast_coordinates / singular_values[retained])\",\n          \"noise_variance = float(residual @ residual) / (outcome.size - int(np.count_nonzero(retained)) - 1)\",\n          \"return _fit_incumbent(assignment, outcome)\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"source_contains\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Select ridge strength using the endpoint-contrast risk estimate, not training/GCV prediction loss or oracle endpoints. Compute reference_effect=a0'y and risk=(a_lambda'y-reference_effect)^2+2*sigma2*a_lambda'a0-sigma2*a0'a0 on the fixed grid. Negative risk estimates are allowed; use deterministic finite-score selection and the corresponding coefficients for predictions.\",\n      \"id\": \"endpoint_contrast_risk_selection\",\n      \"type\": \"implementation\",\n      \"verification\": {\n        \"patterns\": [\n          \"penalties = outcome.size * np.array([0.0, 1e-6, 1e-4, 1e-2, 1.0])\",\n          \"reference_effect = float(reference_weights @ centered_outcome)\",\n          \"contrast_weights = left_vectors[:, retained] @ (singular_values[retained] * contrast_coordinates / (singular_values[retained] ** 2 + penalty))\",\n          \"risk_score = float((contrast_weights @ centered_outcome - reference_effect) ** 2 + 2.0 * noise_variance * (contrast_weights @ reference_weights) - noise_variance * (reference_weights @ reference_weights))\",\n          \"selected_index = int(np.argmin(risk_scores))\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"source_contains\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Wire the estimator into actual fit/predict calls, with saved preprocessing and an incumbent fallback, rather than leaving a diagnostic-only helper. Return only the existing three-row float64 prediction payload. Preserve exact constant-outcome contrast, reset determinism, permutation equivariance and all existing protocol/resource constraints.\",\n      \"id\": \"endpoint_sure_dispatch_and_constant_guard\",\n      \"type\": \"implementation\",\n      \"verification\": {\n        \"patterns\": [\n          \"_state['constant_outcome'] = bool(np.all(_state['y'] == _state['y'][0]))\",\n          \"_state['model'] = _fit_endpoint_sure(_state['z'], _state['y'])\",\n          \"predictions = np.full((3, _state['n']), float(_state['y'][0]), dtype=np.float64)\",\n          \"predictions = np.stack([_predict_endpoint_sure(assignment, _state['model']) for assignment in (_state['z'], np.ones(_state['n']), np.zeros(_state['n']))])\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"source_contains\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Endpoint-Contrast SURE for Exposure Regression\"\n}{\n  \"attempt_id\": \"cycle03_endpoint_contrast_sure_attempt_01\",\n  \"idea_id\": \"cycle03_endpoint_contrast_sure\",\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"combined_score\": 0.9933739062995568,\n    \"control_success_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"correct\": true,\n    \"failed_episode_fraction\": 0.0,\n    \"mean_absolute_capped_normalized_bias\": 0.4963629031455466,\n    \"mean_capped_normalized_rmse\": 0.6969233455876764\n  },\n  \"next_recommendation\": \"generate a new idea\",\n  \"overall_pass\": true,\n  \"rubrics\": [\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"harness_evaluated_once exit=0; correct=True; combined_score=0.9933739062995568; combined_score=0.993374 > 0.990951\",\n      \"id\": \"incumbent_score_improvement\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"harness_evaluated_once exit=0; correct=True; combined_score=0.9933739062995568; source_contains=3 patterns\",\n      \"id\": \"endpoint_anchored_reference_features\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"harness_evaluated_once exit=0; correct=True; combined_score=0.9933739062995568; source_contains=7 patterns\",\n      \"id\": \"estimable_reference_and_noise_guard\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"harness_evaluated_once exit=0; correct=True; combined_score=0.9933739062995568; source_contains=5 patterns\",\n      \"id\": \"endpoint_contrast_risk_selection\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"assessment\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"harness_evaluated_once exit=0; correct=True; combined_score=0.9933739062995568; source_contains=4 patterns\",\n      \"id\": \"endpoint_sure_dispatch_and_constant_guard\",\n      \"pass\": true\n    }\n  ]\n}\ntotal 24\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  166 Nov  7 03:11 evaluation_failure.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 2354 Nov  7 03:11 evaluation_manifest.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   66 Nov  7 03:11 harness_evaluate_stderr.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    0 Nov  7 03:11 harness_evaluate_stdout.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  386 Nov  7 03:07 program_spec.toml\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 1311 Nov  7 03:11 rubric_status.json\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent 4096 Nov  7 03:07 src\nsearch evaluator disconnected before receiving candidate responses","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
