{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --local-memory-md /workspace/paper/memory.md --global-memory-md /workspace/investigation/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl /workspace/investigation/memory.jsonl --event-json '{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Selected a ten-query neighborhood around regression adjustment, endpoint-functional ridge risk, design-based context, and the observed Stanford3 graph. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=This stage organizes existing evidence without adding scientific experiments.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"paper_data.json final evaluation has 24 seeds and 576 scientific cases across four families and six mechanism identifiers, with recorded difference-in-means, own-treatment OLS and one-hop OLS comparators. Reaggregation of recorded uncapped errors shows family/mechanism heterogeneity and no universal dominance over one-hop OLS. Selected source jointly changes hinge features to quadratic exposure features and regularization selection; ablation_studies is empty. Two-hop GCV candidate has no valid comparative result; its local failure log says evaluator disconnected before candidate responses.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Write mirrored Markdown/JSON with explicit no-ablation and no-universal-superiority caveats; prefer allowed starter-title queries and classical statistical theory, exclude neural architectures, unused SNAP graphs, generic optimization and any attempt to identify the restricted paper.\\\"}'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
